=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `on: [push, pull_request]` -> `on: [push]` still runs the suite on every pushed branch
origin: issue #181, spelling 3 as reported — an unfiltered push runs on the pull request's own
origin2: branch, so a same-repository PR keeps its check. Fork pull requests do lose CI; whether
origin3: that alone blocks is an open maintainer question on the issue, so this stays the existing warn.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on: [push, pull_request]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on: [push]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
